            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The 'mini.git' module is not intended as a [fully feature Git client](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b418d585d99bd1c1a4b04dc8b2c585471665173a/doc/mini-git.txt#L25-L27). While 'tpope/vim-fugitive' is more of a fully-featured Git client and seems to have [special handling of this specific command](https://github.com/tpope/vim-fugitive/blob/4a745ea72fa93bb15dd077109afbb3d1809383f2/autoload/fugitive.vim#L5488-L5646) (which is [often the case](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b418d585d99bd1c1a4b04dc8b2c585471665173a/doc/mini-git.txt#L49-L52)).\n\nIn this particular case it seems that executing `git mergetool` in CLI directly would require extra user input (judging by the `Hit return to start merge resolution tool` part of notification ). This is usually not a good fit to be called with `:Git` and indeed is better done via fully featured Git client.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
